    "result_text": "All 10 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I implemented and why.\n\n## The rule\nA new owner's `membershipLevel` is capped at one above the highest membership level among existing members of the same household; with no existing household member, no cap applies.\n\n## Changes\n\n**New pipeline step \u2014 `CapMembershipLevel`** (`rest/function/owner/`): scans existing owners sharing the new owner's household id (reusing `HouseholdNormalizer.belongsTo`), takes the max of their `MembershipLevel.forPoints(MembershipPoints.of(...))`, and stores `max + 1` as the ceiling \u2014 or `null` when there is no household member. Modeled on the sibling `CountHousehold`/`CountNamesakes` steps; single responsibility.\n\n**`Owner`** \u2014 added a persisted `membershipLevelCap` (`membership_level_cap` column, added to all four DB schemas: hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql, since tests run `ddl-auto=none`). The cap is a creation-time snapshot, mirroring how `householdSize`/`namesakeCount` are stored.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`** \u2014 still derives the banded level from points, then holds it down to the stored ceiling (`Math.min(level, cap)` when a cap is present). The derivation stays in `MembershipLevel`; the mapper just wires the derived value to the stored cap.\n\n**`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted `capMembershipLevel` (under `transaction` governance) right after `countHousehold`, before `save`.\n\n## One necessary supporting fix\nThe new test creates two distinct owners in the *same* household, which `EnsureUniqueIdentity` was rejecting as a 409 on household-id alone \u2014 making the cap unobservable. But `FlagPossibleDuplicate`'s own contract already documents that a household member *\"giving a different telephone... is allowed but marked for follow-up\"* \u2014 meaning that branch was unreachable dead code. I aligned `EnsureUniqueIdentity` with that documented design: a hard duplicate is now same household **and** same telephone; distinct household members pass the block (then get flagged and capped). Updated the javadoc on both `EnsureUniqueIdentity` and `DuplicateIdentityException` to match.",
